coule of questions on 3.1 artifacts and alignment compatibilities.
"Spoiler" warning (minor):

Okay, by now it's obvious that certain artifacts are not compatible with
opposite-aligned characters.

But to what extent does it go?  I have #dipped a long sword into a fountain
with a chaotic character and received a cursed-cloud, so I know that won't
work.  But I got a frost-brand (in a shop) with a Lawful character and was
able to use the weapon normally.  Isn't frostbrand a neutral weapon?  When
I wielded it, I got the message "you feel a blast of power from the Frost
Brand" or something like that.  I didn't notice any loss of hit points or
anything though.  

Also, what is the penalty for using a rust weapon?  I went into Croesus'
castle and lost my +3 frostbrand to a nymph.  When I managed to kill off
all of the soldiers, I found my frostbrand in the rubble described as a
"thuroughly rusted +3 frostband."  It did seem to kill monsters less quickly,
but what exactly is the penalty?  Does it come off the "to hit" or "damage"
plus?

